---
interface Props { type: 'distribution-existing' | 'distribution-proposed' | 'processing' | 'rollout' | 'routing' | 'sequencing' }
const { type } = Astro.props;
---
<figure class={`case-diagram diagram-${type}`}>
  {type === 'distribution-existing' && <>
    <figcaption><strong>Existing system</strong><span>Two points materialize the complete dataset</span></figcaption>
    <div class="flow wide" role="img" aria-label="Distributed data store is fully scanned by an export service, serialized and uploaded to object storage, then downloaded and fully materialized in memory by the serving layer.">
      <div class="node source"><small>source</small><b>Distributed<br/>data store</b></div><i aria-hidden="true">full scan →</i>
      <div class="boundary danger"><span>producer</span><div class="node"><b>Export service</b><small>full dataset in memory</small></div><em>memory pressure / OOM</em></div><i aria-hidden="true">serialize →</i>
      <div class="node artifact"><small>artifact</small><b>Object storage</b></div><i aria-hidden="true">download →</i>
      <div class="boundary warn"><span>serving</span><div class="node"><b>Serving layer</b><small>full dataset in memory</small></div><em>complete materialization</em></div>
    </div>
  </>}
  {type === 'distribution-proposed' && <>
    <figcaption><strong>Proposed architecture</strong><span>Local reads keep remote lookups outside the hot path</span></figcaption>
    <div class="flow wide" role="img" aria-label="Data is scanned into an LMDB snapshot, stored and distributed to serving nodes, where a local read-only LMDB supports membership lookups without remote calls in the latency-sensitive hot path.">
      <div class="node source"><small>source</small><b>Data store</b></div><i aria-hidden="true">scan / build →</i>
      <div class="boundary"><span>snapshot build</span><div class="node accent"><b>LMDB snapshot</b><small>compact keys</small></div></div><i aria-hidden="true">upload →</i>
      <div class="node artifact"><b>Object storage</b></div><i aria-hidden="true">distribute →</i>
      <div class="boundary success"><span>serving node</span><div class="node"><b>Local read-only LMDB</b><small>membership lookup</small></div><em>latency-sensitive hot path</em></div>
    </div>
    <p class="diagram-note"><b>Boundary:</b> snapshot distribution and failure semantics remain under architecture review.</p>
  </>}
  {type === 'processing' && <>
    <figcaption><strong>Removing work that the access pattern did not need</strong></figcaption>
    <div class="compare" role="img" aria-label="Before: indexed database ordering passed through sorted pagination and redundant work before processing. After: indexed database ordering passes through regular pagination directly to processing.">
      <section><span>Before</span><div class="mini-flow"><b>Database<br/><small>indexed ordering</small></b><i>→</i><b>Sorted pagination</b><i>→</i><b class="crossed">Redundant sorting / work</b><i>→</i><b>Processing service</b></div></section>
      <section class="after"><span>After</span><div class="mini-flow"><b>Database<br/><small>indexed ordering</small></b><i>→</i><b>Regular pagination</b><i>→</i><b>Processing service</b></div><p>The extra ordering guarantee was unnecessary for this access pattern.</p></section>
    </div>
  </>}
  {type === 'rollout' && <>
    <figcaption><strong>Validation and rollout</strong></figcaption>
    <ol class="steps" aria-label="Validation and rollout sequence"><li><span>01</span><b>Output equivalence</b></li><li><span>02</span><b>Canary</b></li><li><span>03</span><b>Production monitoring</b></li></ol>
  </>}
  {type === 'routing' && <>
    <figcaption><strong>Classification before shared processing</strong><span>Format-specific behavior stays isolated</span></figcaption>
    <div class="route" role="img" aria-label="The existing request path classifies pause inventory early, carries an internal signal through the existing pipeline, and isolates pause-specific matching from normal video behavior before producing a response.">
      <div class="node"><b>Existing request path</b></div><i>→</i><div class="decision"><b>Pause inventory detection?</b><span class="branch normal">normal video → existing matching</span><span class="branch pause">pause → internal semantic signal → isolated matching</span></div><i>→</i><div class="node accent"><b>Response</b><small>existing pipeline</small></div>
    </div>
  </>}
  {type === 'sequencing' && <>
    <figcaption><strong>A sequencing decision, not a rejection of the long-term model</strong></figcaption>
    <div class="sequence" role="img" aria-label="A dedicated model offers cleaner long-term semantics with much larger cross-stack scope. An incremental first release offers smaller scope and faster launch while deliberately accepting future debt.">
      <section><span>Long-term direction</span><h3>Dedicated model now</h3><p>Cleaner semantics</p><p>Much larger cross-stack scope</p></section>
      <div class="sequence-mark"><small>chosen<br/>first</small>→</div>
      <section class="selected"><span>Delivery sequence</span><h3>Incremental first release</h3><p>Smaller scope · faster launch</p><p>Deliberate future debt</p></section>
    </div>
  </>}
</figure>
